  "text": "Hi Northwind Outdoor team, I’m reaching out regarding a recent bulk order for our small outdoor education nonprofit. We purchased $1,500 worth of camping gear and bikes last month, which should have generated 1,500 loyalty points based on your standard rate of 1 point for every $1.00 spent. However, our account shows zero points credited. I understand that bulk or business purchases are often excluded from loyalty programs, and I’m not trying to argue against your general rules. That said, as a small business that relies on these incentives to stretch our limited budget, this discrepancy is a significant hurdle. Could you please review our transaction history? If the points were intentionally withheld due to our business status, I would greatly appreciate it if you could make a one-time exception to credit the 1,500 points. We are committed to being long-term customers and would love to continue supporting your shop. Thank you for considering our request."
